cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Skill Diplomacy: exchange institutions, screening and contamination in
  populations of skill-trading language-model agents
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it. The repository is the
  data-availability statement for the accompanying manuscript: every
  deterministic number regenerates from a single command, and the event logs the
  metrics fold over are committed under runs/logs/.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Löchli"
    given-names: "Roland"
    email: roland.loechli@googlemail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/ReloadLightly/skill-diplomacy"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - artificial life
  - cultural evolution
  - self-improving agents
  - agent skills
  - artificial immune systems
  - horizontal transfer
abstract: >-
  A harness for studying populations of language-model agents that exchange
  Agent-Skills artifacts. Three dials are manipulated — which agents may copy
  from whom, which are willing to give, and what an importer tests before
  keeping what it received — with screening charged to the same token budget as
  self-improvement, so the cost of governance is commensurable with the
  capability it protects. Deterministic results run on the standard library
  alone; live results require a model.
